-ACP state, sessions, and saved project trust live under `~/.bangboo/agent`. Model and thinking-level selection, cancellation, and text/image prompts are supported. Session fork, rename, archive, auto mode, and RPC UI are unsupported. MCP server metadata supplied by the client is accepted for bb compatibility but ignored; Bangboo does not connect to those servers or expose their tools.
+ACP state, sessions, and saved project trust live under `~/.bangboo/agent`. Model and thinking-level selection, cancellation, and text/image prompts are supported. Session fork, rename, archive, auto mode, and RPC UI are unsupported.
+
+`session/new` and `session/load` consume `_meta.lody.sessionConfig` version 1 before returning model and thinking-level options. Invalid structures return `invalidParams`; unknown models and unsupported thinking levels are ignored. Loading without this metadata preserves the saved configuration.
+
+Client `mcpServers` entries connect over stdio or streamable HTTP. Their tools use the same exposure and `mcp__<server>__<tool>` namespace as local MCP servers. Local `mcp.json` entries and package registrations take precedence on name or namespace collisions. Client entries apply only to this session and are never saved to `mcp.json`. Connection failures produce warnings on stderr and do not stop session startup.
 
 ACP mode runs every tool with full permission. Tool calls are never sent to the client for approval. Connect only from clients and projects that you trust.
